1
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:16,040
<i>♪ I know you</i>

2
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:21,360
<i>♪ I walked with you</i>
<i>once upon a dream</i>

3
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:24,080
<i>♪ I know you</i>

4
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:29,360
<i>♪ The gleam in your eyes</i>
<i>is so familiar a gleam</i>

5
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:32,360
<i>♪ Yet I know it's true</i>

6
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:37,200
<i>♪ That visions are seldom</i>
<i>all they seem</i>

7
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:41,800
<i>♪ But if I know you</i>
<i>I know what you'll do</i>

8
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,960
<i>♪ You'll love me at once</i>

9
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:50,840
<i>♪ The way you did</i>
<i>once upon a dream ♪</i>

10
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,440
<i>NARRATOR:</i>
<i>In a faraway land long ago,</i>

11
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,520
<i>lived a king</i>
<i>and his fair queen.</i>

12
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,560
<i>Many years had they longed</i>
<i>for a child,</i>

13
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:13,240
<i>and finally</i>
<i>their wish was granted.</i>

14
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:18,120
<i>A daughter was born,</i>
<i>and they called her Aurora.</i>

15
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,840
<i>♪ Sweet Aurora ♪</i>

16
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,520
<i>NARRATOR:</i>
<i>Yes, they named</i>
<i>her after the dawn,</i>

17
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:31,680
<i>for she filled their</i>
<i>lives with sunshine.</i>

18
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:35,480
<i>Then a great holiday</i>
<i>was proclaimed</i>
<i>throughout the kingdom,</i>

19
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,320
<i>so that all</i>
<i>of high or low estate</i>

20
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:41,520
<i>might pay homage</i>
<i>to the infant princess.</i>

21
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:46,480
<i>And our story begins</i>
<i>on that most joyful day.</i>

22
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:49,600
<i>♪ On that joyful day</i>

23
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:54,880
<i>♪ On that joyful day ♪</i>

24
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:57,040
(BELLS CHIMING)

25
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:00,640
<i>♪ Joyfully now</i>
<i>to our princess we come</i>

26
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:05,400
<i>♪ Bringing gifts</i>
<i>and all good wishes too</i>
<i>we pledge our loyalty anew</i>

27
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:09,560
<i>♪ Hail to</i>
<i>the Princess Aurora</i>

28
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:13,840
<i>♪ All of her subjects</i>
<i>adore her</i>

29
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,160
<i>♪ Hail to the King</i>
<i>Hail to the Queen</i>

30
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:22,520
<i>♪ Hail to</i>
<i>the Princess Aurora</i>

31
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:26,920
<i>♪ Health to the Princess</i>
<i>Wealth to the Princess</i>

32
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:31,120
<i>♪ Long live</i>
<i>the Princess Aurora</i>

33
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,280
<i>♪ Hail, Aurora</i>

34
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,800
<i>♪ Hail, Aurora</i>

35
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:44,240
<i>♪ Health to the Princess</i>
<i>Wealth to the Princess</i>

36
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:48,480
<i>♪ Long live</i>
<i>the Princess Aurora</i>

37
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,680
<i>♪ Hail to the King</i>
<i>Hail to the Queen</i>

38
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:59,520
<i>♪ Hail to</i>
<i>the Princess Aurora ♪</i>

39
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,720
<i>NARRATOR: Thus, on this</i>
<i>great and joyous day</i>

40
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:09,200
<i>did all the kingdom celebrate</i>
<i>the long-awaited royal birth.</i>

41
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,520
<i>And good King Stefan</i>
<i>and his queen</i>

42
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,040
<i>made welcome</i>
<i>their lifelong friend.</i>

43
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,640
(TRUMPETS BLOWING)

44
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,440
Their royal highnesses,

45
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:26,080
King Hubert

46
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,400
and Prince Phillip!

47
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:34,160
<i>NARRATOR: Fondly had</i>
<i>these monarchs dreamed one</i>
<i>day their kingdoms to unite.</i>

48
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,560
<i>Thus, today would they</i>
<i>announce that Phillip,</i>

49
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,480
<i>Hubert's son and heir,</i>

50
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:41,200
<i>to Stefan's child</i>
<i>would be betrothed.</i>

51
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:46,720
<i>And so to her</i>
<i>his gift he brought.</i>

52
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,920
<i>And looked unknowing</i>
<i>on his future bride.</i>

53
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:56,320
(TRUMPETS BLOWING)

54
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:09,120
HERALD:
Their most honored
and exalted excellencies,

55
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,960
the three good fairies!

56
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,480
Mistress Flora!

57
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,880
Mistress Fauna!

58
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,400
And Mistress Merryweather!

59
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,160
Oh.
Oh.

60
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,160
The little darling.

61
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:41,360
FAIRIES: Your Majesties.

62
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:44,720
Each of us
the child may bless
with a single gift,

63
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,400
no more, no less.

64
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:56,200
Little princess,
my gift shall be
the gift of beauty.

65
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,560
<i>♪ One gift</i>

66
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,880
<i>♪ Beauty rare</i>

67
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:13,240
<i>♪ Gold of sunshine</i>
<i>in her hair</i>

68
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:21,040
<i>♪ Lips that shame</i>
<i>the red, red rose</i>

69
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:28,680
<i>♪ She'll walk with springtime</i>
<i>wherever she goes ♪</i>

70
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:40,680
Tiny princess,
my gift shall be
the gift of song.

71
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,720
<i>♪ One gift</i>

72
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:54,200
<i>♪ The gift of song</i>

73
00:06:55,120 --> 00:07:00,480
<i>♪ Melody her whole life long</i>

74
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:07,880
<i>♪ The nightingale's</i>
<i>her troubadour</i>

75
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:15,720
<i>♪ Bringing his sweet serenade</i>
<i>to her door ♪</i>

76
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,840
Sweet princess,
my gift shall be...

77
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,920
(WIND HOWLING)

78
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,640
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

79
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,440
FAUNA:
Why, it's Maleficent.

80
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:54,360
What does she want here?
Shh.

81
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:58,360
Well, quite a glittering
assemblage, King Stefan.

82
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,640
Royalty, nobility,

83
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,280
the gentry and...

84
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:07,920
(CHUCKLES)
How quaint.

85
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:09,880
Even the rabble.

86
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,520
(GRUNTS IN ANGER)

87
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:14,880
I really felt
quite distressed at not
receiving an invitation.

88
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,960
You weren't wanted.

89
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,560
Not want...

90
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:22,480
(CHUCKLES)
Oh, dear, what an
awkward situation.

91
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:26,560
I had hoped
it was merely due
to some oversight.

92
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:29,520
Well, in that event,
I'd best be on my way.

93
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:33,400
And, you're
not offended,
Your Excellency?

94
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:35,640
Why, no, Your Majesty.

95
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,600
And to show
I bear no ill will,

96
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:43,400
I, too, shall bestow
a gift on the child.

97
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,560
Listen well, all of you.

98
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:53,800
The princess shall indeed
grow in grace and beauty,

99
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,320
beloved by
all who know her.

100
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,640
But,

101
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,080
before the sun sets
on her 16th birthday,

102
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:12,120
she shall prick her finger on
the spindle of a spinning
wheel and die!

103
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,400
Oh, no!

104
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:14,920
(CACKLING)

105
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,960
Seize that creature!

106
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,040
Stand back, you fools!

107
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,200
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

108
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,360
(EVIL LAUGHTER)

109
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:33,200
Don't despair,
Your Majesties.

110
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,680
Merryweather still
has her gift to give.

111
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:39,720
Then she can undo
this fearful curse?

112
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,360
Oh, no, sire.

113
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:44,720
Maleficent's powers
are far too great.

114
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,480
But she can help.

115
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,800
But...

116
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,520
FAUNA:
Just do your best, dear.

117
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:52,760
FLORA: Yes, go on.

118
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,400
Sweet princess,

119
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:59,360
if through this
wicked witch's trick

120
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:01,920
<i>a spindle should</i>
<i>your finger prick,</i>

121
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:06,760
<i>a ray of hope there</i>
<i>still may be in this,</i>
<i>the gift I give to thee.</i>

122
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:10,960
<i>Not in death,</i>
<i>but just in sleep.</i>

123
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:13,400
<i>The fateful prophecy</i>
<i>you'll keep.</i>

124
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,960
<i>And from this slumber</i>
<i>you shall wake,</i>

125
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,840
<i>when true love's kiss</i>
<i>the spell shall break.</i>

126
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:24,400
<i>♪ For true love</i>

127
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:30,600
<i>♪ Conquers all ♪</i>

128
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:33,280
<i>NARRATOR:</i>
<i>But King Stefan,</i>

129
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:36,040
<i>still fearful of</i>
<i>his daughter's life,</i>

130
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:39,960
<i>did then and there decree</i>
<i>that every spinning wheel</i>
<i>in the kingdom</i>

131
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:43,200
<i>should on that</i>
<i>very day be burned.</i>

132
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,800
<i>So it was done.</i>

133
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,040
Oh, silly fiddle-faddle.

134
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:09,120
Now,
come have a nice
cup of tea, dear.

135
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,320
I'm sure it'll
work out somehow.

136
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,240
Well,
a bonfire won't
stop Maleficent.

137
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:16,680
Of course not.
But what will?

138
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,880
Well,
perhaps if we
reason with her.

139
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:21,000
Reason?
With Maleficent?

140
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:24,920
Well, she can't
be all bad.
Oh, yes, she can!

141
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,320
Oh, I'd like to turn her
into a fat, old hoptoad.

142
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:32,680
Now, dear,
that isn't a very
nice thing to say.

143
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,080
Besides, we can't.

144
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,360
You know our magic
doesn't work that way.

145
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:40,040
It can only do good, dear,
to bring joy and happiness.

146
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,960
Well, that would
make me happy.

147
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:44,640
But there must be some way.

148
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:48,280
There is!
There is?

149
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,680
What is it, Flora?

150
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,440
I'm going to...

151
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:55,000
Shh, shh, shh, shh.
Even walls have ears.

152
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,720
Follow me.

153
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:19,680
I'll turn her
into a flower.
Maleficent?

154
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:22,480
(GIGGLES)
Oh, no, dear.
The princess.

155
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:25,000
Oh, she'd make
a lovely flower.

156
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:27,920
Don't you see?
A flower can't
prick its finger.

157
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,360
It hasn't any.
That's right.

158
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,000
FLORA: She'll be
perfectly safe.

159
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:34,200
Until Maleficent
sends a frost.

160
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:37,000
(LAUGHS) Yes, uh...

161
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:38,480
Oh, dear.

162
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:41,840
She always ruins
your nicest flowers.

163
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,120
You're right.

164
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:46,040
And she'll be
expecting us to do
something like that.

165
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:51,280
(GROANS) Well, what
won't she expect?
She knows everything.

166
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,160
Oh, but she doesn't, dear.

167
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:56,160
Maleficent
doesn't know
anything about love,

168
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:59,640
or kindness or the joy
of helping others.

169
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:04,400
You know, sometimes
I don't think she's
really very happy.

170
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,960
That's it!

171
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:09,600
Of course.
It's the only thing
she can't understand

172
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,280
and won't expect.

173
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:15,280
(GIGGLING)
Now, now, we'll have
to plan it carefully.

174
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:19,240
Let's see.
The woodcutter's cottage,
yes, yes, the abandoned one.

175
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:21,840
Of course, the King
and Queen will object.

176
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:24,240
But when we explain
it's the only way...

177
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,040
(ECHOING)
Explain what?

178
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:31,640
About
the three peasant women
raising a foundling child

179
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,800
deep in the forest.

180
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:37,120
Oh, that's
very nice of them.

181
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,600
Who are they?

182
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,240
Turn around.

183
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:42,920
(GASPING)

184
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,520
Why, it's us!

185
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,600
Uh-huh.

186
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,000
You mean, "we" us?

187
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,040
Uh-huh.

188
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,480
Take care of the baby?

189
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:50,720
FLORA: Why not?

190
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:53,240
FAUNA:
Oh, I'd like that.

191
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,800
(STUTTERS) Well, yes,
but we'd have to feed it.

192
00:13:55,880 --> 00:14:00,720
And wash it and dress it
and rock it to sleep.
Oh, I'd love it.

193
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,240
You really think we can?

194
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,480
If humans can do it,
so can we.

195
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,720
And we'd have our
magic to help us.

196
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,240
FAUNA: That's right.

197
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:11,240
No, no, no, no, no!
No magic.

198
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:13,760
I'll take those
wands right now.

199
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:16,080
Oh, better get rid
of those wings, too.

200
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:20,240
You mean live
like mortals?
For 16 years?

201
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,720
FLORA: Uh-huh.

202
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,440
Now, now,
we don't know how.

203
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:26,480
We've never
done anything
without magic.

204
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,840
That's why Maleficent
will never suspect.

205
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,320
But who'll wash?

206
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,720
And cook?
Oh, we'll all pitch in.

207
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,000
I'll take care
of the baby.

208
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,960
Let me have it, dear.

209
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Come along now. We must
tell Their Majesties
at once.

210
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:45,880
Flora?

211
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:48,040
MERRYWEATHER: Flora?

212
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:56,560
<i>NARRATOR:</i>
<i>So, the King and his queen</i>
<i>watched with heavy hearts</i>

213
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:58,640
<i>as their most</i>
<i>precious possession,</i>

214
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,160
<i>their only child,</i>

215
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:02,560
<i>disappeared into the night.</i>

216
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:18,040
<i>Many sad and lonely</i>
<i>years passed by</i>

217
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:21,560
<i>for King Stefan</i>
<i>and his people.</i>

218
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:25,840
<i>But as the time</i>
<i>for the princess's</i>
<i>16th birthday drew near,</i>

219
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,480
<i>the entire kingdom</i>
<i>began to rejoice.</i>

220
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:33,240
<i>For everyone knew that as</i>
<i>long as Maleficent's domain,</i>

221
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:38,120
<i>the Forbidden Mountains,</i>
<i>thundered with her wrath</i>
<i>and frustration,</i>

222
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,440
<i>her evil prophecy</i>
<i>had not yet been</i>
<i>fulfilled.</i>

223
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,160
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

224
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,440
It's incredible!

225
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:59,520
Sixteen years,
and not a trace of her!

226
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:02,200
She couldn't have
vanished into thin air!

227
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:06,480
Are you sure
you searched
everywhere?

228
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:10,760
(SNORTS) Yes, uh, yes,
everywhere. We all did.

229
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,040
Yes, yes.

230
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,440
(ALL BABBLING)

231
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:16,640
And what about the town?
The forest? The mountains?

232
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:20,000
Uh, we searched mountains,
forests...

233
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,560
And houses and, uh...

234
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,720
Let me see.
And all the cradles.

235
00:16:25,800 --> 00:16:27,040
Cradle?

236
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:29,000
(LAUGHS) Yep, yep.

237
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:31,040
Every cradle.

238
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,440
Cradle!

239
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,440
Did you hear
that, my pet?

240
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:40,640
All these years they've
been looking for a baby.

241
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,720
(HYSTERICAL LAUGHTER)

242
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,920
(LAUGHING)

243
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,960
(ALL LAUGHING)

244
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,400
Fools!

245
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,560
(SNORTS)

246
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:58,560
Idiots! Imbeciles!

247
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:02,280
(ALL SCREAMING)

248
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:08,400
(GROANING)

249
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:10,480
(SIGHS IN DISAPPOINTMENT)

250
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,960
Oh, they're hopeless.

251
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:18,880
A disgrace to
the forces of evil.

252
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,960
(SIGHS) My pet.

253
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,600
You are my last hope.

254
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:29,280
Circle far and wide.

255
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:31,800
Search for a maid of 16,

256
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:36,480
with hair of sunshine gold
and lips red as the rose.

257
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:40,640
Go, and do
not fail me.

258
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:48,600
<i>NARRATOR: And so,</i>
<i>for 16 long years,</i>

259
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:52,200
<i>the whereabouts</i>
<i>of the princess</i>
<i>remained a mystery.</i>

260
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,400
<i>While deep in the forest,</i>
<i>in a woodcutter's cottage,</i>

261
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:59,200
<i>the good fairies carried out</i>
<i>their well-laid plan.</i>

262
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:02,920
<i>Living like mortals,</i>
<i>they had reared the</i>
<i>child as their own,</i>

263
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,200
<i>and called her Briar Rose.</i>

264
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,840
(HUMMING)

265
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:15,160
<i>NARRATOR: On this,</i>
<i>her 16th birthday, the good</i>
<i>fairies had planned a party.</i>

266
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:18,680
<i>And something extra</i>
<i>special for a surprise.</i>

267
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,240
Well, how about
this one?

268
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,600
This is the one
I picked.

269
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,720
Oh, she'll look
beautiful in that.

270
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,440
Now, I thought
a few changes here.
Uh-huh.

271
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,600
FAUNA: Don't forget
a pretty bow.

272
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:31,080
Yes, and raise
the shoulder line.

273
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:33,320
We'll make it blue.
Oh, no, dear, pink.

274
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,320
But...
Of course,
we need a few pleats.

275
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,600
MERRYWEATHER:
Yes, but how are we gonna
get her out of the house?

276
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,880
FLORA:
I'll think of something.

277
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,000
(FAIRIES GIGGLING)

278
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:43,920
Well, and what are you
three dears up to?

279
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,200
Up to?
Up to?

280
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,280
Up to?

281
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,640
(STAMMERING)
Well, well, we...

282
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,560
We want you to
pick some berries.

283
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,280
That's it! Berries!
Berries?

284
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:59,280
Lots of berries.
But I picked
berries yesterday.

285
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,320
FLORA: Oh, we need more, dear.

286
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,040
FAUNA: Lots, lots more.

287
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,520
FLORA: (GIGGLES) Yes.

288
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,800
Now, don't hurry back, dear.
But don't go too far.

289
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,480
And don't speak
to strangers.

290
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,640
FAUNA: Goodbye, dear.

291
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,040
MERRYWEATHER: Goodbye.
FLORA: Goodbye.

292
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:14,640
Goodbye.

293
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:18,320
I wonder
if she suspects.

294
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,880
Of course not.
Come on.

295
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,480
(LAUGHING)
Will she be surprised.

296
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:27,400
A real birthday party.
With a real birthday cake.

297
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:30,880
Yes, and a dress
a princess can
be proud of.

298
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,280
I'll get the wands.

299
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:34,960
Yes, you can, uh...
The wands?

300
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:36,200
Oh, no!

301
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,800
FLORA: No magic!

302
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,240
But the 16 years
are almost over.

303
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,240
We're taking no chances.

304
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:45,520
But I've never baked
a fancy cake.

305
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,560
Oh, you won't
have to, dear.

306
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,680
I'm going to
bake the cake.

307
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:52,400
You?
Now, she's always
wanted to, dear.

308
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,960
And this is
her last chance.
Well...

309
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,880
I'm going to make it
15 layers with pink
and blue forget-me-nots.

310
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:01,440
And I'm making
the dress.

311
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:04,280
But you can't sew,
and she's never cooked.

312
00:20:04,320 --> 00:20:08,040
(LAUGHING) It's simple.
All you do is
follow the book.

313
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,680
Up here, dear.
You can be the dummy.

314
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,840
Well, I still say
we ought to use magic.

315
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,680
(LAUGHS)

316
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,200
(HUMMING)

317
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,240
(HUMMING)

318
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,640
"Flour, three cups."

319
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:27,680
Cups, cups, cups,
cups, cups, cups.

320
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:29,680
Oh.

321
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:31,440
(HUMMING)

322
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:34,160
One, two, three.

323
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:36,160
What's that for?

324
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,600
Well, it's got to have
a hole in the bottom.

325
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:41,400
FAUNA: That's for
the feet to go through.

326
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:47,760
It's pink!
Oh, lovely shade,
isn't it?

327
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:49,680
But I wanted it blue.

328
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,520
(GRUNTS)
Now, dear,

329
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,720
we decided pink
was her color.

330
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:55,680
You decided!

331
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,960
(CHUCKLES)

332
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,960
(GRUNTING)

333
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:01,120
(MUTTERING ANGRILY)

334
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:07,560
(HUMMING)

335
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:10,760
"Two eggs, fold in gently."

336
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,000
Fold? Oh, well.

337
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:16,880
(HUMMING)

338
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:18,960
(SHELLS CRACKING)

339
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,120
(MUFFLED)
I can't breathe!

340
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,800
Let me out of here.

341
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:30,280
It looks awful.
That's because
it's on you, dear.

342
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,800
"Now, yeast, one tsp."

343
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:33,880
"Tsp?"

344
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:36,120
One teaspoon.

345
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:38,160
(GIGGLING) Oh,
one teaspoon,
of course.

346
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,520
(HUMMING)

347
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:48,960
Oh, gracious,
how that child
has grown.

348
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,760
Oh, it seems
only yesterday
we brought her here.

349
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:54,480
Just a tiny baby.

350
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,200
(SNIFFLES)

351
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,400
Why, Merryweather.

352
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,400
Whatever is
the matter, dear?

353
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:04,480
(CRYING) After today
she'll be a princess,

354
00:22:04,520 --> 00:22:06,120
and we won't have
any Briar Rose.

355
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,880
Oh, Flora.
Now, now, now, now.

356
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:13,720
Well, we all knew
this day had to come.

357
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,800
But why did it have
to come so soon?

358
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:20,640
After all,
we've had her
for 16 years.

359
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:23,160
Sixteen wonderful years.

360
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,600
(SNIFFLES)

361
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,400
(CLEARS THROAT)

362
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:30,040
Oh, gracious!
We're acting like
a lot of ninnies.

363
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:33,240
Come on. She'll be back
before we get started.

364
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,600
(VOCALIZING)

365
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:51,600
(CHIRPING TO THE SAME TUNE)

366
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,520
(AURORA VOCALIZING)

367
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,520
(CHIRPING)

368
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:08,120
(VOCALIZING)

369
00:23:11,840 --> 00:23:13,600
(BOTH CHIRPING)

370
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,960
(VOCALIZING)

371
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:28,240
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

372
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:36,960
(VOCALIZING CONTINUES)

373
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:46,320
(HOOTING)

374
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:50,160
(HOOTING)

375
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:52,000
(VOCALIZING)

376
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,560
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

377
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:20,120
(AURORA VOCALIZING)

378
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:22,120
You hear that, Samson?

379
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:23,920
Beautiful.

380
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,240
(SNORTS)

381
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,800
What is it?

382
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:32,800
Come on. Let's find out.

383
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:35,640
(SNORTS)
Aw, come on.

384
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:38,840
For an extra
bucket of oats?

385
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:41,600
And a few carrots?

386
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,520
Hup, boy!

387
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:57,360
(AURORA VOCALIZING)

388
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,400
PHILLIP: Whoa!

389
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:17,680
(SNORTS)

390
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,400
(WATER SPLASHING)

391
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:31,200
No carrots.

392
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:35,120
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

393
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,840
(HUMMING)

394
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,640
♪ I wonder

395
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,800
♪ I wonder

396
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:55,400
♪ I wonder why
each little bird

397
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:58,160
♪ Has a someone

398
00:25:58,160 --> 00:26:00,480
♪ To sing to

399
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:04,400
♪ Sweet things to

400
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:10,720
♪ A gay little love melody

401
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:15,360
♪ I wonder

402
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:18,440
♪ I wonder

403
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,920
♪ If my heart keeps singing

404
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:26,160
♪ Will my song go winging

405
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:28,720
♪ To someone

406
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:32,600
♪ Who will find me

407
00:26:33,280 --> 00:26:38,720
♪ And bring back a love song

408
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:43,680
♪ To me ♪

409
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,280
(SIGHS) Oh, dear.

410
00:26:50,120 --> 00:26:52,960
Why do they still
treat me like a child?

411
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,440
Who?

412
00:26:57,320 --> 00:27:01,280
Aunt Flora and Fauna
and Merryweather.

413
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:06,040
They never want me
to meet anyone.

414
00:27:08,800 --> 00:27:11,760
(GIGGLES)
But you know something?

415
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:16,680
(WHISPERING)
I fooled them.
I have met someone.

416
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,840
(BIRDS TWITTERING)

417
00:27:17,920 --> 00:27:19,320
Who?

418
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:23,800
Who? Who?

419
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:27,040
Oh... A prince.

420
00:27:30,040 --> 00:27:33,240
Well, he's tall
and handsome and...

421
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:36,280
And so romantic.

422
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:38,280
(CHIRPING)

423
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:42,720
Oh, we walk together
and talk together.

424
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,280
And just before
we say goodbye,

425
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:49,640
he takes me in his arms,

426
00:27:50,320 --> 00:27:51,440
and then...

427
00:27:51,560 --> 00:27:53,040
(EXCITED CHIRPING)

428
00:27:53,520 --> 00:27:55,080
I wake up.

429
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,920
(DEJECTED CHIRPING)

430
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:00,400
Yes, it's only
in my dreams.

431
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:02,400
(SNIFFLES)

432
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:07,120
But they say if you dream
a thing more than once,
it's sure to come true.

433
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:09,840
And I've seen him
so many times.

434
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:14,280
(AURORA HUMMING)

435
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,280
(HOOTING)

436
00:28:39,280 --> 00:28:40,920
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

437
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:54,320
PHILLIP: You know, Samson,

438
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:57,360
there was something
strange about that voice.

439
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:01,000
Too beautiful to be real.

440
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:05,720
Maybe it was a mysterious
being, a wood sprite, or...

441
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:07,200
(SNORTS)

442
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:08,800
(NEIGHS)

443
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:10,360
Here, stop!

444
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:35,480
(HUMMING)

445
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:39,000
(OWL HOOTING)

446
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,120
(GASPS)

447
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:43,400
AURORA: Why,
it's my dream prince.

448
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,200
(GIGGLING)

449
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:48,840
Your Highness.

450
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:51,520
(HUMMING)

451
00:29:55,800 --> 00:29:59,080
You know, I'm really
not supposed to speak
to strangers.

452
00:29:59,120 --> 00:30:01,280
But we've met before.

453
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:04,040
♪ I know you

454
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:08,480
♪ I walked with you
once upon a dream

455
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:12,120
♪ I know you

456
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:18,040
♪ The gleam in your eyes
is so familiar a gleam

457
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:21,600
♪ Yet I know it's true

458
00:30:21,680 --> 00:30:26,520
♪ That visions are
seldom all they seem

459
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:29,040
♪ But if I know you

460
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:31,720
♪ I know what you'll do

461
00:30:31,760 --> 00:30:35,200
♪ You'll love me at once

462
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:42,160
♪ The way you did
once upon a dream

463
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:46,440
♪ La, la, la, la, la

464
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:53,720
♪ But if I know you

465
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:56,760
♪ I know what you'll do

466
00:30:56,840 --> 00:30:59,600
♪ You'll love me at once

467
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:01,480
♪ The way you did
♪ The way you...

468
00:31:01,560 --> 00:31:06,360
♪ Once upon a dream ♪

469
00:31:06,440 --> 00:31:07,640
(HOOTING)

470
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:09,680
Oh. Oh!

471
00:31:10,440 --> 00:31:13,720
I'm awfully sorry.
I didn't mean to
frighten you.

472
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:16,280
Oh, it...
Wasn't that.

473
00:31:16,360 --> 00:31:19,120
It's just that
you're, uh, uh...

474
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:20,400
A stranger?

475
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:24,120
AURORA: Mmm-hmm.
PHILLIP: But don't you
remember? We've met before.

476
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:27,880
We... We have?
Well, of course.
You said so yourself.

477
00:31:27,960 --> 00:31:29,880
Once upon a dream.

478
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:32,600
♪ I know you

479
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:37,360
♪ I walked with you
once upon a dream

480
00:31:38,360 --> 00:31:41,040
♪ I know you

481
00:31:41,120 --> 00:31:47,040
♪ The gleam in your eyes
is so familiar a gleam

482
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:53,880
<i>♪ And I know it's true</i>

483
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:59,000
<i>♪ That visions are seldom</i>
<i>all they seem</i>

484
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:03,080
<i>♪ But if I know you</i>

485
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:06,040
<i>♪ I know what you'll do</i>

486
00:32:06,080 --> 00:32:09,440
<i>♪ You'll love me at once</i>

487
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:13,240
<i>♪ The way you did once</i>

488
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:20,320
<i>♪ Upon a dream ♪</i>

489
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:29,280
Who are you?
What's your name?

490
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:32,120
Hmm?

491
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:34,840
Oh! My name.

492
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,720
Why, it's, it's...

493
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:40,800
Oh, no, no.
I can't. I...

494
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:43,880
Goodbye.
But when will
I see you again?

495
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,920
Oh, never, never!

496
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:47,640
PHILLIP: Never?

497
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:51,400
Well, maybe someday.
When? Tomorrow?

498
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:54,320
Oh, no!
This evening!

499
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:57,640
Where?
At the cottage in the glen.

500
00:33:02,760 --> 00:33:04,520
(HUMMING)

501
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:08,280
There. Whoop!

502
00:33:14,640 --> 00:33:16,360
Well, what do you
think of it?

503
00:33:16,440 --> 00:33:17,960
Why, it's...

504
00:33:18,040 --> 00:33:21,120
It's a very unusual
cake, isn't it?

505
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:25,440
Yes.
Of course, it'll be much
stiffer after it's baked.

506
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:26,880
Of course, dear.

507
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:29,520
Um, what do you
think of the dress?

508
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:31,560
Well, it's...

509
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:35,040
It's not exactly the way
it is in the book, is it?

510
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:40,560
Oh, I improved it.
But perhaps if I added
a few more ruffles...

511
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:44,280
What do you think?
Um, I think so.

512
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:47,040
What do you think,
Merryweather?

513
00:33:47,120 --> 00:33:51,120
I think
we've had enough
of this nonsense!

514
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:55,280
I think we ought to
think of Rose and what
she'll think of this mess.

515
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:58,320
I still think
what I thunk before.

516
00:33:58,400 --> 00:34:00,560
I'm going to
get those wands.

517
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:05,520
You know,
I think she's right.

518
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:06,880
(FOOTSTEPS PATTERING)

519
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:09,120
Here they are, good as new!

520
00:34:09,200 --> 00:34:12,600
(STUTTERING)
Careful, Merryweather.

521
00:34:13,600 --> 00:34:15,480
Quick, lock the doors.

522
00:34:16,640 --> 00:34:18,520
Fauna, you close
the windows.

523
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:21,400
Oh, block up
every cranny.

524
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:23,520
We can't take any chances.

525
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:27,560
And now, you take
care of the cake.

526
00:34:27,640 --> 00:34:30,040
While I...
Clean the room, dear.

527
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:32,600
And I'll make the dress.

528
00:34:32,680 --> 00:34:34,520
Now hurry!
Ooh!

529
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:39,440
Come on,
bucket, mop, broom.

530
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,720
Flora says
clean up the room.

531
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:50,880
(MERRYWEATHER GIGGLES)

532
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:53,400
And now to make
a lovely dress,

533
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:55,720
fit to grace
a fair princess.

534
00:34:58,240 --> 00:35:00,400
♪ Eggs, flour, mi... ♪

535
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:05,280
Just do it like it
says here in the book.
I'll put on the candles.

536
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:02,200
Oh, no, not pink.

537
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:03,680
Make it blue.

538
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:05,800
(GASPS)
Merryweather!

539
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:08,120
Make it pink.

540
00:36:11,640 --> 00:36:13,680
(WHISPERS)
Make it blue.

541
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:16,320
Oh, pink.

542
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:20,600
Blue.

543
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:48,280
(SQUAWKING)

544
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:58,640
(SQUAWKING)

545
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:15,640
(EXCLAIMS) Now look
what you've done!

546
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:17,280
(AURORA HUMMING)

547
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:18,880
Shh. Listen.

548
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:22,400
It's Rose.
She's back.

549
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:24,640
Enough of
this foolishness.

550
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:30,240
Make it pink.
Now, hide, quick!

551
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:35,360
(WHISPERS) Blue.

552
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:37,120
Aunt Flora!

553
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:42,560
Good gracious!
Who left the mop running?

554
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:45,120
(GASPS) Stop, mop.

555
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:51,440
Aunt Flora, Fauna,
Merryweather.

556
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:56,560
Where is everybody?

557
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:57,960
(GASPS)

558
00:37:58,120 --> 00:37:59,240
Oh!

559
00:37:59,280 --> 00:38:01,600
FAIRIES: Surprise!

560
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:03,160
Happy birthday!

561
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:04,800
Oh, you darlings.

562
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:07,600
This is the happiest day
of my life.

563
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:11,800
Everything's so wonderful.
Just wait till you meet him.

564
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:14,480
Him?
Rose.

565
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:17,280
You...
You've met some stranger?

566
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:20,800
Oh, he's not a stranger.
We've met before.

567
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:22,960
You have?
Where?

568
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:24,800
Once upon a dream.

569
00:38:25,640 --> 00:38:28,160
♪ I know you

570
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:32,440
♪ I walked with you
once upon a dream ♪

571
00:38:33,840 --> 00:38:36,000
She's in love.

572
00:38:36,040 --> 00:38:38,200
Oh, no.
This is terrible.

573
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:42,400
Why?
After all, I am 16.

574
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:44,000
It isn't that, dear.

575
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:47,200
You're already betrothed.
Betrothed?

576
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:49,000
Since the day you were born.

577
00:38:49,040 --> 00:38:51,080
To Prince Phillip, dear.

578
00:38:51,160 --> 00:38:55,160
But that's impossible.
How could I marry a prince?

579
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:57,040
I'd have to be...
A princess.

580
00:38:57,120 --> 00:38:58,480
And you are, dear.

581
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:00,560
Princess Aurora.

582
00:39:00,640 --> 00:39:04,400
Tonight,
we're taking you back to
your father, King Stefan.

583
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:08,280
But... But I can't.
He's coming here tonight.

584
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,560
I promised to meet him.

585
00:39:10,600 --> 00:39:12,520
I'm sorry, child,

586
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:15,680
but you must never see
that young man again.

587
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:18,200
Oh, no! No!

588
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:20,400
I can't believe it!

589
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:22,440
(CRYING) No!

590
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:30,440
And we thought
she'd be so happy.

591
00:39:31,040 --> 00:39:32,200
(SOBBING)

592
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:45,960
(DEEP SIGH)

593
00:39:46,640 --> 00:39:48,120
No sign of her yet, Hubert.

594
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:50,440
Course not.

595
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:53,560
It's a good half hour
till sunset.

596
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:58,720
(BELCHES)
Ah, excellent bird.

597
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,520
Mmm.

598
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:03,840
Oh, now, come, man!

599
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:06,520
Buck up! Battle's over!

600
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:08,720
Girl's as good as here.

601
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:13,320
I'm sorry, Hubert,
but after 16 years
of worrying,

602
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:15,400
never knowing...
The past!

603
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:17,080
All in the past.

604
00:40:23,480 --> 00:40:26,000
Tonight,
we toast the future,

605
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:29,880
with something
I've been saving
for 16 years.

606
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:31,520
(CHUCKLES)

607
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:36,440
Here, to the future.

608
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:38,720
STEFAN:
Right, Hubert.
To the future.

609
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:41,200
(KINGS LAUGHING)

610
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:44,440
♪ Skumps, skumps

611
00:40:44,520 --> 00:40:47,120
♪ Skumps
♪ A toast to this night

612
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:50,880
♪ The outlook is rosy
♪ And the future is bright

613
00:40:50,960 --> 00:40:55,000
BOTH:
♪ Our children will marry
Our kingdoms unite

614
00:40:55,080 --> 00:40:57,240
♪ Skumps, skumps

615
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,800
♪ Skumps ♪

616
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:06,320
HUBERT: (SIGHS)
Ah, excellent vintage.

617
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:08,720
(HUBERT CHUCKLING)

618
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,120
(HICCUPS)

619
00:41:11,520 --> 00:41:14,960
And now,
to the new home, eh?
New home?

620
00:41:15,040 --> 00:41:17,640
Children need a nest
of their own, what?

621
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:19,840
Place to raise their
little brood, eh?

622
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:21,040
(HUBERT CHUCKLES)

623
00:41:21,120 --> 00:41:23,360
STEFAN:
Well, I suppose in time...

624
00:41:23,400 --> 00:41:25,680
HUBERT: Of course!
To the home!

625
00:41:26,280 --> 00:41:27,920
♪ Skumps
♪ Skumps

626
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:29,840
♪ A toast to the home

627
00:41:29,880 --> 00:41:33,440
♪ One grander by far
than a palace in Rome

628
00:41:33,520 --> 00:41:37,440
Now, let me
fill up your glass.
That last was all foam.

629
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:40,000
♪ Skumps, skumps
♪ Skumps, skumps

630
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:42,280
♪ Skumps ♪

631
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:43,840
(KINGS SLURPING)

632
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:45,720
(KINGS LAUGHING)

633
00:41:47,040 --> 00:41:48,560
(HUBERT CLAPS)

634
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,440
The plans!

635
00:41:56,560 --> 00:41:57,560
(HICCUPS)

636
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:58,880
Well, what do you think?

637
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,880
Nothing elaborate,
of course.

638
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:02,960
Forty bedrooms, dining hall.

639
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:04,960
Honeymoon cottage, really.

640
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:07,960
You... You mean,
you're building
it already?

641
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,120
Built, man! Finished!

642
00:42:10,200 --> 00:42:12,120
Lovebirds can
move in tomorrow.

643
00:42:12,200 --> 00:42:16,120
Tomorrow?
But, Hubert, they're
not even married yet.

644
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:18,040
(LAUGHS) Take care
of that tonight.

645
00:42:18,120 --> 00:42:20,640
To the wedding!
Now, hold on, Hubert.

646
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:23,120
I haven't
even seen my
daughter yet,

647
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:25,120
and you're taking her
away from me.

648
00:42:25,160 --> 00:42:27,640
HUBERT: Getting my
Phillip, aren't you?
STEFAN: Yes, but...

649
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:30,800
HUBERT: Want to see our
grandchildren, don't we?
Of course, but...

650
00:42:30,880 --> 00:42:32,720
There's no time to lose.

651
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,040
Getting on in years.

652
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:35,480
(LAUGHING)

653
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:37,280
To the wedding!

654
00:42:37,320 --> 00:42:39,480
STEFAN: Now,
be reasonable,
Hubert.

655
00:42:39,520 --> 00:42:43,120
After all, Aurora knows
nothing about all this.

656
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:44,200
Well?

657
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:47,840
Well, it may come
as quite a shock.

658
00:42:47,920 --> 00:42:49,520
(GAGS) Shock?

659
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:52,200
My Phillip, a shock?

660
00:42:52,880 --> 00:42:55,440
What's wrong
with my Phillip?

661
00:42:55,520 --> 00:42:58,080
Nothing, Hubert.
I only meant...

662
00:42:58,160 --> 00:43:01,240
Why doesn't your
daughter like my son?

663
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:04,320
Now, now...
I'm not so sure

664
00:43:04,360 --> 00:43:07,080
my son likes
your daughter!

665
00:43:07,160 --> 00:43:10,720
Now, see here.
I'm not so sure
my grandchildren

666
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:13,200
want you for
a grandfather!

667
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:16,480
Why, you,
you unreasonable...
Huh?

668
00:43:16,560 --> 00:43:19,320
...pompous, blustering,
old windbag!
Who? Uh...

669
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:22,480
Unreasonable, pompous,
<i>en garde,</i> sir!

670
00:43:22,560 --> 00:43:25,320
I warn you, Hubert.
This means war.

671
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:29,600
Forward! For honor!
For country! For...

672
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:32,000
(BOTH LAUGHING)

673
00:43:37,840 --> 00:43:39,440
What's this
all about anyway?

674
00:43:39,520 --> 00:43:43,960
(CHUCKLES)
Nothing, Hubert.
Absolutely nothing.

675
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:46,360
Children bound to fall
in love with each other.

676
00:43:46,800 --> 00:43:49,520
Precisely. And as
for grandchildren,

677
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:53,840
I'll have the royal
woodcarvers start work
on the cradle tomorrow.

678
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:56,520
Splendid!
King-size, of course.

679
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:59,280
Certainly.
To the woodcarvers' guild.

680
00:43:59,320 --> 00:44:01,360
(LUTE STRINGS VIBRATING)

681
00:44:07,440 --> 00:44:10,280
(SNORING)

682
00:44:10,960 --> 00:44:12,600
(LUTE VIBRATING)

683
00:44:13,040 --> 00:44:17,120
MAN: His royal highness
Prince Phillip!

684
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:18,360
Phillip?

685
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:19,920
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

686
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:27,360
Phillip!
Phillip!

687
00:44:28,880 --> 00:44:30,720
Phillip, ho, Phillip!

688
00:44:37,200 --> 00:44:39,200
(PANTING)
Hurry, boy, hurry.

689
00:44:39,280 --> 00:44:41,400
Change into
something suitable.

690
00:44:41,440 --> 00:44:43,960
Can't meet your future
bride looking like that.

691
00:44:44,040 --> 00:44:45,520
But I have met her, Father.

692
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:47,600
You have? Where?

693
00:44:47,640 --> 00:44:49,120
Once upon a dream.

694
00:44:49,200 --> 00:44:50,320
(HUMMING)

695
00:44:50,400 --> 00:44:53,520
Oh, Phillip, stop it.
Stop that! Phillip!

696
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:55,840
Put me down.

697
00:44:55,920 --> 00:44:59,000
Now, what's all this
dream nonsense?

698
00:44:59,080 --> 00:45:01,960
It wasn't a dream, Father.
I really did meet her.

699
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:03,160
Princess Aurora?

700
00:45:03,240 --> 00:45:05,120
Good heavens,
we must tell Stefan.

701
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:08,280
Why, this is the most...
I didn't say it was Aurora.

702
00:45:08,320 --> 00:45:09,960
You most certainly did.
You said...

703
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:12,560
I said, I met the girl
I was going to marry.

704
00:45:12,640 --> 00:45:15,200
I don't know who she was.
A peasant girl, I suppose.

705
00:45:15,280 --> 00:45:17,120
(STUTTERING) A peasant girl?

706
00:45:17,200 --> 00:45:20,800
You're going to marry a...
Why, Phillip.

707
00:45:20,840 --> 00:45:23,080
(NERVOUS LAUGH)
You're joking.

708
00:45:26,200 --> 00:45:27,440
Isn't he?

709
00:45:29,600 --> 00:45:32,960
No! You can't
do this to me!

710
00:45:33,040 --> 00:45:35,040
Give up the throne,
the kingdom,

711
00:45:35,080 --> 00:45:37,440
for some, some nobody?

712
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:40,080
By Harry,
I won't have it!

713
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:44,040
You're a prince,
and you're going
to marry a princess!

714
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:46,000
Now, Father,
you're living
in the past.

715
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:48,200
This is the 14th century.
Nowadays...

716
00:45:48,240 --> 00:45:50,560
Nowadays,
I'm still the king

717
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:52,840
and I command you
to come to your senses!

718
00:45:52,880 --> 00:45:54,800
And marry
the girl I love?
Exactly!

719
00:45:54,880 --> 00:45:56,760
Goodbye, Father.
Goodbye, Father.

720
00:45:56,840 --> 00:45:58,600
Marry the girl you...
No, no!

721
00:45:58,680 --> 00:46:01,360
No, no, Phillip!
Stop! Come back!

722
00:46:01,400 --> 00:46:02,720
Oh, Phillip!

723
00:46:08,080 --> 00:46:10,080
(ECHOING) Phillip!

724
00:46:30,040 --> 00:46:31,440
(GROANS) Oh, ho.

725
00:46:31,520 --> 00:46:34,000
Oh, how will I
ever tell Stefan?

726
00:47:20,960 --> 00:47:23,160
(WHISPERING)
Come along now.

727
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:37,360
All right.
In here, dear.

728
00:47:41,280 --> 00:47:42,400
(SIGHS)

729
00:47:42,440 --> 00:47:44,160
FLORA:
Bolt the door,
Merryweather.

730
00:47:44,240 --> 00:47:46,120
Fauna,
pull the drapes.

731
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:50,360
And now, dear,
if you'll just
sit here.

732
00:47:52,080 --> 00:47:55,360
This one last gift,
dear child, for thee.

733
00:47:56,680 --> 00:47:58,680
The symbol
of thy royalty.

734
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:02,960
A crown to wear
in grace and beauty

735
00:48:03,640 --> 00:48:06,360
as is thy right
and royal duty.

736
00:48:08,760 --> 00:48:11,200
(SOBBING)

737
00:48:11,240 --> 00:48:12,800
Now, dear...

738
00:48:13,560 --> 00:48:14,680
Come.

739
00:48:17,040 --> 00:48:19,360
Let her have
a few moments alone.

740
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:22,280
It's that boy she met.

741
00:48:22,680 --> 00:48:24,360
Whatever are we
going to do?

742
00:49:05,080 --> 00:49:09,960
Oh, I don't see why
she has to marry
any old prince.

743
00:49:10,040 --> 00:49:13,440
Now, that's not for
us to decide, dear.

744
00:49:25,360 --> 00:49:28,680
Maybe we should
tell King Stefan
about the boy.

745
00:49:28,760 --> 00:49:30,080
Well, why don't we?

746
00:49:30,120 --> 00:49:34,000
Listen! Maleficent!
Rose!

747
00:49:34,080 --> 00:49:36,080
ALL: (GASPING) Rose!

748
00:49:36,200 --> 00:49:38,400
FAUNA: Oh, why did
we leave her alone?

749
00:49:38,480 --> 00:49:40,080
ALL: Rose!

750
00:49:58,680 --> 00:50:00,400
(ALL GRUNTING)

751
00:50:00,840 --> 00:50:02,200
Here.

752
00:50:02,240 --> 00:50:04,160
ALL: Rose!

753
00:50:04,200 --> 00:50:07,240
ALL: Rose. Where are you?

754
00:50:13,880 --> 00:50:16,480
ALL: (ECHOING) Rose!

755
00:50:29,560 --> 00:50:31,480
(ECHOING) Rose!

756
00:50:31,560 --> 00:50:33,000
Rose!

757
00:50:43,800 --> 00:50:45,280
ALL: Rose!

758
00:50:55,800 --> 00:51:00,280
FAUNA: Rose!
FLORA: (ECHOING) Rose,
don't touch anything!

759
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:04,160
MALEFICENT:
Touch the spindle.

760
00:51:04,560 --> 00:51:06,240
Touch it, I say!

761
00:51:08,880 --> 00:51:10,560
(ALL GASPING)

762
00:51:11,080 --> 00:51:16,560
You poor, simple fools,
thinking you could defeat me!

763
00:51:16,640 --> 00:51:19,840
Me!
The mistress of all evil!

764
00:51:21,320 --> 00:51:24,880
Well, here's your
precious princess!

765
00:51:25,880 --> 00:51:28,280
(SINISTER LAUGHTER)

766
00:51:31,520 --> 00:51:32,960
Rose.
Oh, Rose.

767
00:51:34,480 --> 00:51:39,120
FLORA: (CRYING)
Oh, I'll never
forgive myself.

768
00:51:40,080 --> 00:51:42,600
FAUNA: (CRYING)
We're all to blame.

769
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:48,280
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

770
00:51:51,560 --> 00:51:52,960
Stefan, there's...

771
00:51:53,040 --> 00:51:55,560
There's
something important
I have to tell you.

772
00:51:55,600 --> 00:51:57,640
Not now, Hubert.

773
00:51:57,760 --> 00:51:59,680
But it's about Phillip.

774
00:51:59,800 --> 00:52:02,840
Phillip? Oh, yes,
of course, Phillip.

775
00:52:02,920 --> 00:52:04,800
Why, where is the boy?

776
00:52:04,880 --> 00:52:06,920
That's what I'm
trying to tell you.

777
00:52:07,280 --> 00:52:09,280
Well, send for him
immediately!
But...

778
00:52:09,320 --> 00:52:10,640
Shh!

779
00:52:10,680 --> 00:52:13,120
(TRUMPETS BLOWING)

780
00:52:13,160 --> 00:52:15,440
HERALD: The sun has set!

781
00:52:15,480 --> 00:52:18,880
Make ready to welcome
your princess!

782
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:21,200
(CROWD CHEERING)

783
00:52:38,120 --> 00:52:39,840
(ALL SOBBING)

784
00:53:19,920 --> 00:53:23,360
Poor King Stefan
and the Queen.

785
00:53:23,440 --> 00:53:26,240
They'll be heartbroken
when they find out.

786
00:53:29,040 --> 00:53:32,280
They're not going to.
MERRYWEATHER:
They aren't? But...

787
00:53:32,320 --> 00:53:36,480
We'll put them all to
sleep until Rose awakens.

788
00:53:43,680 --> 00:53:44,760
Come.

789
00:53:53,240 --> 00:53:59,760
<i>♪ Sleeping beauty fair</i>

790
00:54:00,960 --> 00:54:04,880
<i>♪ Gold of sunshine</i>

791
00:54:04,920 --> 00:54:09,040
<i>♪ In your hair</i>

792
00:54:10,160 --> 00:54:13,200
<i>♪ Lips that shame</i>

793
00:54:13,280 --> 00:54:18,480
<i>♪ The red, red rose</i>

794
00:54:18,560 --> 00:54:21,880
<i>♪ Dreaming of true love</i>

795
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:27,240
<i>♪ In slumber repose</i>

796
00:54:27,880 --> 00:54:31,840
<i>♪ One day</i>

797
00:54:31,920 --> 00:54:36,080
<i>♪ He will come</i>

798
00:54:36,120 --> 00:54:42,360
<i>♪ Riding out of the dawn</i>

799
00:54:44,960 --> 00:54:47,960
<i>♪ And you'll awaken</i>

800
00:54:48,040 --> 00:54:52,320
<i>♪ To love's first kiss</i>

801
00:54:53,200 --> 00:54:57,880
<i>♪ Till then, sleeping beauty</i>

802
00:54:57,960 --> 00:55:01,960
<i>♪ Sleep on</i>

803
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:06,600
<i>♪ One day you'll awaken</i>

804
00:55:07,360 --> 00:55:12,560
<i>♪ To love's first kiss</i>

805
00:55:12,640 --> 00:55:19,440
<i>♪ Till then, sleeping beauty</i>

806
00:55:20,720 --> 00:55:25,680
<i>♪ Sleep on ♪</i>

807
00:55:25,880 --> 00:55:28,440
(YAWNING)

808
00:55:34,040 --> 00:55:37,560
Well, just been
talking to Phillip.

809
00:55:37,640 --> 00:55:42,000
Seems he's fallen
in love with some
peasant girl.

810
00:55:42,440 --> 00:55:44,040
Peasant girl?

811
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:46,720
Yes? Yes?

812
00:55:48,560 --> 00:55:49,640
The peasant girl?

813
00:55:49,720 --> 00:55:51,760
Who is she?
Where did he meet her?

814
00:55:52,400 --> 00:55:55,240
Just some peasant girl
he met...

815
00:55:55,280 --> 00:55:56,960
Where? Where?

816
00:55:57,560 --> 00:56:01,560
(YAWNING)
Once upon a dream.

817
00:56:01,600 --> 00:56:03,360
Once upon a...

818
00:56:03,440 --> 00:56:06,960
Rose! Prince Phillip!
Oh! Oh!

819
00:56:11,440 --> 00:56:14,720
Come on. We've got to
get back to the cottage.

820
00:56:34,320 --> 00:56:37,640
(WHISTLING <i>ONCE UPON A DREAM)</i>

821
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:03,480
WOMAN: Come in.

822
00:57:08,240 --> 00:57:09,920
(GOONS BABBLING)

823
00:57:17,280 --> 00:57:18,880
(GRUNTING)

824
00:57:20,960 --> 00:57:23,000
(CAWING)

825
00:57:33,280 --> 00:57:34,400
Well!

826
00:57:35,600 --> 00:57:38,080
This is
a pleasant surprise.

827
00:57:39,120 --> 00:57:41,440
I set my trap
for a peasant

828
00:57:41,440 --> 00:57:44,640
and, lo,
I catch a prince!

829
00:57:44,680 --> 00:57:46,680
(CACKLING)

830
00:57:48,120 --> 00:57:50,320
Away with him.

831
00:57:50,400 --> 00:57:53,200
But gently, my pets. Gently.

832
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:55,440
(GOONS GRUNTING)

833
00:57:55,520 --> 00:57:59,240
I have plans
for our royal guest.

834
00:58:26,800 --> 00:58:28,200
(ALL GASP)

835
00:58:31,280 --> 00:58:33,760
ALL: (GASPING) Maleficent!

836
00:58:33,840 --> 00:58:36,440
She's got Prince Phillip.

837
00:58:36,480 --> 00:58:37,880
At the Forbidden Mountain.

838
00:58:37,920 --> 00:58:42,200
(GASPING)
But we can't,
we can't go there.

839
00:58:43,120 --> 00:58:45,240
We can,
and we must!

840
01:00:17,320 --> 01:00:18,440
(SNORTS)

841
01:00:27,960 --> 01:00:29,640
(GOONS CHATTERING)

842
01:00:41,800 --> 01:00:44,080
(GOONS CHATTERING)

843
01:01:07,160 --> 01:01:10,360
What a pity
Prince Phillip
can't be here

844
01:01:10,480 --> 01:01:12,400
to enjoy
the celebration.

845
01:01:12,520 --> 01:01:13,960
(CHUCKLING)

846
01:01:15,200 --> 01:01:16,560
Come.

847
01:01:16,600 --> 01:01:19,520
We must go
to the dungeon
and cheer him up.

848
01:02:13,520 --> 01:02:16,040
Oh, come now,
Prince Phillip.

849
01:02:16,120 --> 01:02:18,160
Why so melancholy?

850
01:02:19,040 --> 01:02:21,680
A wondrous future
lies before you.

851
01:02:22,360 --> 01:02:25,240
You, the destined hero

852
01:02:25,320 --> 01:02:28,560
of a charming
fairy tale come true.

853
01:02:33,120 --> 01:02:36,400
Behold,
King Stefan's castle.

854
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:39,440
And in yonder
topmost tower

855
01:02:39,800 --> 01:02:42,040
dreaming of
her true love,

856
01:02:42,760 --> 01:02:45,400
the Princess Aurora.

857
01:02:46,880 --> 01:02:49,280
But see
the gracious
whim of fate.

858
01:02:50,160 --> 01:02:53,560
(CHUCKLES) Why, 'tis
the selfsame peasant
maid

859
01:02:53,600 --> 01:02:57,360
who won the heart of our
noble prince but yesterday.

860
01:03:00,600 --> 01:03:04,600
She is indeed
most wondrous fair.

861
01:03:05,880 --> 01:03:08,720
Gold of sunshine
in her hair.

862
01:03:08,840 --> 01:03:12,240
Lips that shame
the red, red rose.

863
01:03:13,240 --> 01:03:17,640
In ageless sleep
she finds repose.

864
01:03:19,960 --> 01:03:22,400
The years roll by.

865
01:03:22,480 --> 01:03:27,040
But a hundred years
to a steadfast heart
are but a day.

866
01:03:27,680 --> 01:03:31,600
And now, the gates
of the dungeon part

867
01:03:31,680 --> 01:03:35,480
and our prince is
free to go his way.

868
01:03:36,200 --> 01:03:40,400
Off he rides
on his noble steed

869
01:03:40,480 --> 01:03:44,720
a valiant figure,
straight and tall

870
01:03:44,840 --> 01:03:50,400
to wake his love
with love's first kiss

871
01:03:50,480 --> 01:03:55,880
and prove that
true love conquers all!

872
01:03:55,960 --> 01:03:57,640
(CACKLING)

873
01:03:59,040 --> 01:04:00,680
Why, you, you...

874
01:04:05,440 --> 01:04:06,920
Come, my pet.

875
01:04:06,960 --> 01:04:11,320
Let us leave our noble prince
with these happy thoughts.

876
01:04:16,360 --> 01:04:18,960
A most gratifying day.

877
01:04:24,200 --> 01:04:27,440
For the first time
in 16 years

878
01:04:27,480 --> 01:04:29,760
I shall sleep well.

879
01:04:46,160 --> 01:04:48,040
(WHISPERING) Shh!
No time to explain.

880
01:04:57,760 --> 01:04:59,560
Wait, Prince Phillip.

881
01:04:59,640 --> 01:05:03,720
The road to true love
may be barred by still
many more dangers

882
01:05:03,840 --> 01:05:06,200
which you alone
will have to face.

883
01:05:06,240 --> 01:05:09,680
So arm thyself with this
enchanted Shield of Virtue.

884
01:05:10,920 --> 01:05:13,360
And this mighty
Sword of Truth.

885
01:05:14,280 --> 01:05:17,880
For these weapons of
righteousness will
triumph over evil.

886
01:05:18,680 --> 01:05:20,640
Now, come.
We must hurry.

887
01:05:24,640 --> 01:05:26,080
(SQUAWKING)

888
01:05:26,160 --> 01:05:27,680
(CAWING)

889
01:05:35,680 --> 01:05:37,480
(GOONS SHOUTING)

890
01:05:55,480 --> 01:05:56,920
(NEIGHING)

891
01:05:59,720 --> 01:06:01,240
(SQUAWKING)

892
01:06:04,920 --> 01:06:06,320
(NEIGHING)

893
01:06:08,480 --> 01:06:10,240
Phillip, watch out!

894
01:06:17,280 --> 01:06:18,680
(CAWING)

895
01:06:34,160 --> 01:06:36,200
(CAWING)

896
01:06:41,440 --> 01:06:42,880
(CAWING)

897
01:06:46,040 --> 01:06:47,560
(CAWING)

898
01:07:06,440 --> 01:07:07,480
Silence!

899
01:07:08,680 --> 01:07:11,840
You, tell those
fools to... No!

900
01:07:11,920 --> 01:07:13,280
(GASPS) No!

901
01:07:18,000 --> 01:07:20,120
FAUNA:
Watch out, Phillip!

902
01:07:27,960 --> 01:07:29,960
Hurry!
Hurry, Phillip!

903
01:07:30,040 --> 01:07:31,800
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

904
01:07:37,920 --> 01:07:39,320
(NEIGHING)

905
01:07:42,840 --> 01:07:45,840
A forest of thorns
shall be his tomb.

906
01:07:46,720 --> 01:07:50,360
Borne through the skies
on a fog of doom!

907
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:53,840
Now go with a curse
and serve me well.

908
01:07:53,880 --> 01:07:58,360
Around Stefan's castle,
cast my spell!

909
01:08:15,640 --> 01:08:17,040
(NEIGHING)

910
01:08:17,640 --> 01:08:19,400
(CACKLING)

911
01:08:32,480 --> 01:08:33,920
(NEIGHING)

912
01:08:48,320 --> 01:08:50,640
No! It cannot be!

913
01:08:55,280 --> 01:08:57,160
(NEIGHING)

914
01:08:57,280 --> 01:09:01,080
Now shall you deal with me,
O Prince.

915
01:09:01,200 --> 01:09:04,000
And all the powers of hell!

916
01:09:06,200 --> 01:09:08,000
(CACKLING)

917
01:09:33,200 --> 01:09:34,600
(NEIGHING)

918
01:09:36,640 --> 01:09:38,080
(GRUNTING)

919
01:09:49,120 --> 01:09:50,840
Up! Up this way!

920
01:10:06,320 --> 01:10:07,440
(SINISTER LAUGHTER)

921
01:10:07,480 --> 01:10:10,360
Now, Sword of Truth,
fly swift and sure.

922
01:10:10,480 --> 01:10:13,560
That evil die
and good endure!

923
01:10:13,640 --> 01:10:15,080
(SCREAMING)

924
01:10:40,040 --> 01:10:41,440
(SNORTING)

925
01:11:51,680 --> 01:11:53,200
(ALL YAWNING)

926
01:11:56,040 --> 01:11:58,080
Oh, uh...

927
01:11:58,160 --> 01:12:01,520
Forgive me, Hubert.
The wine. Now, uh...

928
01:12:01,560 --> 01:12:04,200
(CLEARS THROAT)
You were saying?

929
01:12:04,280 --> 01:12:07,680
Huh? I was?
Oh, oh, yes.

930
01:12:07,760 --> 01:12:09,880
(CLEARS THROAT)
Well, huh.

931
01:12:09,960 --> 01:12:13,200
After all, Stefan,
this is the 14th century.

932
01:12:13,280 --> 01:12:16,720
Yes. You said that
a moment ago.

933
01:12:16,760 --> 01:12:19,600
Well, to come
right to the point.

934
01:12:19,680 --> 01:12:22,320
My son Phillip says
he's going to marry...

935
01:12:22,760 --> 01:12:24,600
(TRUMPETS BLOWING)

936
01:12:48,280 --> 01:12:50,640
It's Aurora!
She's here!

937
01:12:55,280 --> 01:12:57,160
(STUTTERS) And Phillip!

938
01:13:12,360 --> 01:13:15,200
What does this mean, boy?

939
01:13:15,280 --> 01:13:17,240
I don't...

940
01:13:20,880 --> 01:13:22,360
But...

941
01:13:24,960 --> 01:13:27,680
<i>(ONCE UPON A DREAM</i> PLAYING)

942
01:13:29,680 --> 01:13:31,520
I don't understand.

943
01:13:54,840 --> 01:13:56,480
(SNIFFLING)

944
01:13:56,560 --> 01:13:59,720
Why, Fauna.
What's the matter, dear?

945
01:13:59,760 --> 01:14:03,680
Oh, I just love
happy endings.

946
01:14:03,760 --> 01:14:06,120
Yes, I do, too.

947
01:14:06,200 --> 01:14:08,200
(EXCLAIMS) Blue?

948
01:14:13,080 --> 01:14:14,280
Pink!

949
01:14:14,400 --> 01:14:17,040
<i>♪ I know you</i>

950
01:14:17,120 --> 01:14:18,480
<i>♪ I walked with you</i>

951
01:14:18,600 --> 01:14:22,160
<i>♪ Once upon a dream</i>
(WHISPERS) Blue!

952
01:14:22,480 --> 01:14:25,360
<i>♪ I know you</i>

953
01:14:25,480 --> 01:14:30,800
<i>♪ The gleam in your eyes</i>
<i>is so familiar a gleam</i>

954
01:14:30,840 --> 01:14:33,680
<i>♪ Yet I know it's true</i>

955
01:14:33,760 --> 01:14:38,280
<i>♪ That visions are seldom</i>
<i>all they seem</i>

956
01:14:38,520 --> 01:14:43,200
<i>♪ But if I know you</i>
<i>I know what you'll do</i>

957
01:14:43,240 --> 01:14:47,480
<i>♪ You'll love me at once</i>
<i>the way you did once</i>

958
01:14:47,520 --> 01:14:50,080
<i>♪ Upon</i>

959
01:14:50,160 --> 01:14:56,440
<i>♪ A dream ♪</i>

